;; The module _asyncio (queue 224; Modules/_asynciomodule.c of CPython 3.14.10): the C Future and Task, FutureIter,
;; TaskStepMethWrapper, the running loop and current task of each thread, the task registry and the call graph's
;; awaited-by sets. The functions follow the C file's, in its order, under the same names in Go's spelling. What C has
;; from its object model (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "Design: 224"): a Future or Task is an *Instance whose last slot
;; is a *futObj (not its value: unwrap would hand the state for the object), which never points back at it (Go does
;; not free a cycle through a finalized object); tp_finalize is the
;; built-in __del__ under finalize.go's workDel; the linked list of tasks, whose references are borrowed, is a short
;; strong list plus a mark in finalize.go's records, which hold no reference.

